  "details": "<p>Hattusa is the former capital of the Hittite empire, a Bronze Age civilization of Anatolia. The site is noted for its remarkable architecture and for its urban layout. Occupied as early as the sixth millennium BC, the site was eventually abandoned ca. 1200 BC.</p>",
